  "about": "The character directory's link messages (docs/network/02-link-protocol.md section 7). Every `ok` frame must read as its type, and a write of what was read must hold every field of the frame with the same value and read back unchanged; where an `ok` case gives `expect`, the message read must have those field values, by the meaning of each field (a profile's fields by their path, a list's by its length). Every `later` frame must read, leaving out what it adds, as a later version may add fields. A reader of the directory's messages alone skips every `unknown` frame, the other link messages among them; every `malformed` frame is refused. In a frame, `${c*N}` stands for the character c written N times.",
